1. fastconformer-quran-ar-juge-int8.onnx  (release fastconformer-quran-ar-juge-v1)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

  fastconformer-quran-ar
  by mohammed
  https://huggingface.co/mohammed/fastconformer-quran-ar
  (revision 60973918b40c5fcdc0e93310c13a4a4661525142,
   file phase3_full_wer0.0014.nemo, sha256
   dc3557eea22b25ab5c7af2d8cf01636efd415c4ed417418156e5895056c705d5)
  Licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
  License (CC-BY-4.0, see LICENSE-CC-BY-4.0,
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).

which is itself a fine-tuned version of:

  stt_ar_fastconformer_hybrid_large_pcd_v1.0
  by NVIDIA
  https://huggingface.co/nvidia/stt_ar_fastconformer_hybrid_large_pcd_v1.0
  (revision 7f32349d952f42a28dce979ba73270aa2bbdfa89)
  Licensed under CC-BY-4.0.

Modifications made in this repository:

  - Only the CTC head of the hybrid model is kept. The encoder and the CTC
    decoder were exported to ONNX with NeMo 3.0.0 (full-context attention,
    no cache, opset 17).
  - The weights of the MatMul operators were quantized to int8 with
    onnxruntime.quantization.quantize_dynamic (onnxruntime 1.31.0,
    op_types_to_quantize=["MatMul"], weight_type=QInt8). The other
    weights stay in float32.
  - NeMo's audio preprocessor (pre-emphasis 0.97, 512-point Fourier
    transform with a 400-sample Hann window and a 160-sample hop, 80 mel
    filters, natural logarithm with a 2^-24 guard, per-feature
    normalization) was rewritten with standard ONNX operators, the Fourier
    transform as a convolution, and placed in front of the encoder. It
    matches NeMo to within 3.1e-5.
  - An ArgMax over the vocabulary and a Cast to int32 were appended, so
    that the model outputs one token index per 80 ms frame.

No weights were retrained. The quantization changes the model's outputs
slightly (about 97 % of the frames keep the same token as the float32
model).

